It is Saturday evening and I am in my flat.
Today I am making something special for dinner.
I am making a Mexican dish.
But I am using my new Indian spices in it.
I bought these spices from the market just yesterday.
I chop tomatoes, onions, and garlic.
I cook them in a large pan.
Then I add some cumin and red chilli to it.
In Mexico too, we use cumin a lot.
But the fragrance of the spices here is very different and nice.
A very familiar smell is filling the whole kitchen.
This fragrance reminds me of my home.
This recipe is a blend of Mexico and Mumbai.
Back then, I didn't know much about the vegetables and spices here.
But now I have gotten used to these things.
Now this city also feels like my home to me.
My fusion food is almost ready.
My friend Asha is going to arrive in a short while.
I set two plates on the table and wait for her.
